---
style: |
  body {
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding: 48px 24px 24px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  
  .staging-frames {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  
  /* The trigger sits at the board's top right so the below-end panel opens
     into the board's room. */
  .staging-anchor {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: var(--space-8);
  }
  
  /* Staging contents only — the panel's interior belongs to whatever surface
     composes a popover, so this stands in for one. */
  .staging-contents {
    width: 240px;
    padding: var(--space-16);
  }
  
  .board {
    position: relative;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  
  .board::before {
    content: attr(data-label);
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 100%;
    left: 0;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #999;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
script: |
  import "../lib/foundation.ts";

  // The invoker is named explicitly: a popover shown by script has no invoker,
  // and the invoker is what the placement anchors to.
  document.querySelector("#open-popover").showPopover({
    source: document.querySelector('button[popovertarget="open-popover"]'),
  });
---
<!--
  The popover spec staged as a frame (staging, not spec content).

  There is no template to render: a popover is the platform's element with the
  foundation's chrome, so the markup below is the whole of it. What is being
  judged is specs/ui/foundation/panels/panels.css.

  The Demo trigger is live — popovertarget is the entire toggle, and outside
  press or Escape dismisses. The Open board shows the panel presented, via
  showPopover(): openness is a runtime state, not markup, so staging shows it
  the way it shows any behavioural state.
-->



<div class="staging-frames">
  <div class="board" data-label="Demo" style="width: 360px; height: 220px">
    <div class="staging-anchor">
      <button popovertarget="demo-popover">Open popover</button>
      <div id="demo-popover" popover placement="bottom-end">
        <div class="staging-contents">A popover: the platform's panel with the foundation's chrome. Press outside, or Escape, to dismiss.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="board" data-label="Open" style="width: 360px; height: 220px">
    <div class="staging-anchor">
      <button popovertarget="open-popover">Open popover</button>
      <!-- manual, as staging apparatus: an auto popover would be closed the
           moment the Demo one opens — the platform keeps one auto popover at a
           time per document, and every board here shares one. -->
      <div id="open-popover" popover="manual" placement="bottom-end">
        <div class="staging-contents">The presented state, shown by script rather than a press.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
